# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
*.egg-info

# The two interpreters, and the reason there are two.
#
# `.env-venv/` runs the harness: nle (which is a compiled NetHack 3.6.6) and the
# gymnasium version it pins, plus what run.py and act.py need. It is the
# interpreter run.py is launched under, so `act` in a workspace inherits it, and
# that is how the daemon ends up holding a NetHack process. Rebuilt by
# tools/make_env_venv.sh.
#
# `.agent-venv/` is what the workspace's `python` shim points at: numpy and
# Pillow and nothing else, so that `import nle` from it fails. The package ships
# the whole game — a second copy to consult offline, the glyph table, every
# object and monster by name — so handing over the harness's own interpreter
# would hand over an oracle. Rebuilt by tools/make_agent_venv.sh.
.venv
.env-venv/
.agent-venv/

# NetHack writes a recording wherever it is started from unless told otherwise.
*.ttyrec*
*.xlogfile

# Secrets — never committed
.env

# Live workspaces, at the root only
/runs/
